ing I  have a t-shirt challenge that I'm  probably going to post a video later but  then later on  had this guy by the name of Alaskan Blue  Jay on YouTube who I met through two  make-a-wish Foundation while I was at  VidCon and I promised him that I would  bring him on board for the livestream  and I almost forgot  but thankfully I've got friends that  reminded me to call him in and we called  him and we had a nice discussion and he  told this story this really really  impactful story that resonated  throughout the rest of the stream then  I'll try to do it justice right now he  probably heard it he didn't make it up  or north neither did I but it's the  story of this young child walks along  the beach and on this Beach  hundreds of starfish wash on shore  doomed to dry out and die but this child  walks along and every time he sees one  he picks one up and he throws it back  into view giving it another chance of  life he can't get to all of them but  every morning this child on his way to  wherever he's going  picks up another starfish and tosses it  back in the game and he does this every  day for a while day by day walking along  the beach tossing another starfish back  in and one day this old man has been  seeing him do this comes up to the child  and asks why are you doing this hundreds  and hundreds of starfish wash up on the  shore every day and you can never save  all of them why even bother you're not  making a difference and the child looked  at the man and looked down the ground at  a starfish at his feet he picked up that  starfish and tossed it back in the ocean  and said it mattered to that one and  that's the story and it's a simple story  with a simple message meaning that if  you do something even in the grand  scheme of the huge insurmountable  obstacle that is the bigger problem if  you chip in just a little bit it will go  so far but then almost immediately after  he told that story we were just talking  there he started screaming J Alaskan  Blue Jay started screaming through the  phone and we didn't know what to make of  it I thought maybe the TV will  it was like a joke or a prank I had no  idea but what happened was his  defibrillator in his chest went off  right on a stream and it scared the crap  huh it scared the crap out of everybody  everyone in stream was so scared and I  didn't really know what to do I tried to  stay calm about the situation he went to  the hospital immediately I tried to stay  in contact with him as of right now I  believe he has had home resting It was  as he was told it was probably a  malfunction more than something  life-threatening but they are monitoring  him and he is doing okay and as an aside  if you could send some love to him he  has a YouTube channel Alaskan Blue Jay  I'll put a link in the description but  the point here is after that story was  told and after he went to the hospital  after that big scare  Catherine helped start this campaign of  $1 donations we had $100,000 goal for  this charity livestream to go to  AbleGamers and we were behind if we were  actually behind and then Catherine kind  of like started this march of dollars  where if someone donated we could see  who donated and if they left a comment  she asked that they comment starfish and  for those of you don't know Catherine is  my editor and good friend and they  commented starfish and after that not  only did the chat take it upon  themselves to start the hashtag pray for  Jay but also do really really rallied  around this concept that these $1  donations could make all the difference  in the world and then we solved like the  counter steadily rocket up names were  flying by everyone who's saying starfish  people were donating for other people in  saying here's 20 starfish here's a  hundred starfish someone donated a  thousand dollars and was like here  here's starfish for everybody that  couldn't be there and can donate and it  was this beautiful beautiful thing this  avalanche of $1 donation the the  representation of what that meant in the  face of being scared for Jay  and after there I kept up with them he  gave us an update when he went to the  hospital he tried to stay on the screen  he tried to like actually watch the  screen while he was in the hospital  which I applaud that so much and and it  was this beautiful beautiful thing that  came out of mages meeting this one guy  and him telling a simple story and  everyone chipping in $1 donations and  without that I don't even know if we  would have made our goal and this all  tied in to the question why do I make  promises that I can't keep because I  made a promise to Jay that I would bring  him on the stream and I almost forgot  not out of maliciousness but just  because I got caught up with other  things and I got busy and I allowed  myself to become complacent and I don't  mean to turn his tragedy into something  that it's not  but without that I don't think we would  have had the drive to keep going I don't  think it would have resonated as hard as  it did and so when I asked myself why do  I make promises that I can't keep and I  think about the answer that I gave on  stage all of that is [ __ ] if I make  a promise and I don't keep it  I am [ __ ] because if I didn't keep  my promise what would we have missed out  on I wouldn't have been able to talk to  Jay and get to know him and you guys  wouldn't know his story and we may not  have made our goal and how many times in  the past have I made promises that I  didn't keep and what opportunities did I  miss because of that I don't want to do  that ever again  I'm almost 28 I'm going to be 28 in two  days here and I do not want to live my  life making promises that are empty in  all the ambition and all the the swept  up nature of the tour and going doing  these ambitious projects and going to  VidCon and going to conventions meeting  people and doing other quote-unquote  bigger projects I  I feel like I've lost sight of the small  things made it 